---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Reference Workflow — Scientific Agentic Engineering"
  description="Scope of the Reference Workflow: a structured exercise applying the Scientific Agentic Engineering framework to build a weather-model error-statistics application."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <p class="text-sm font-medium text-blue-600 uppercase tracking-wide">Milestone 1 · Scope</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900">The Reference Workflow</h1>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        <strong class="text-gray-900">The Reference Workflow</strong> is a structured half-day
        exercise in which you use the AI tooling of your choice to build a small weather-model
        error-statistics application — parsing MET-style verification output, computing and
        converting skill statistics, and visualizing model performance — while applying the
        Scientific Agentic Engineering framework&rsquo;s full loop:
        <em>frame &rarr; plan &rarr; critique &rarr; implement &rarr; verify &rarr; gate &rarr; record</em>.
      </p>

      <p>
        Each stage pairs your build with a deliberately flawed reference implementation embodying
        <em>real, documented</em> failure modes from actual AI-assisted development — unit
        confusion, precision loss, misleading aggregation, visualization misinterpretation — so
        you practice catching them with the framework&rsquo;s tools: validation loops, unit
        checkers, fresh-context adversarial review, and human gates, with a self-grading oracle
        to prove it.
      </p>

      <div class="border-l-4 border-blue-200 bg-blue-50 rounded-r-lg px-5 py-4 text-sm text-gray-600">
        Planned to ship with a synthetic, schema-faithful dataset (clearly labeled, generator and
        seed included) and validators from the SAE Community Repository. Releases
        <strong class="text-gray-900">October 2026</strong> (Milestone&nbsp;2); details may evolve
        with pilot results and community feedback at US-RSE&rsquo;26.
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 pt-4">How it fits the project</h2>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-gray-900">Milestone 1</strong> (July 2026) — this scope, alongside
          the framework draft.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-gray-900">Milestone 2</strong> (October 2026) — the exercise
          releases, together with the Community Repository whose validators it uses.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-gray-900">Milestone 3</strong> (January 2027) — the tutorial series
          <em>Building Your First Scientific Agent</em> guides participants through a validated
          agentic solution to this same workflow.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
